# nr-tui-editor: integration fragment

New crate `native/core/crates/mixdog-tui` (the terminal UI: prompt editor now, the application state machines in the later
tasks of the nr-tui area). Nothing in it was compiled by its author (no cargo in the task); the lead compiles it with the wave.

## native/core/Cargo.toml

In `[workspace] members`, after `"crates/mixdog-tui-style",` (keep the list sorted the way it is):

    "crates/mixdog-tui",

In `[workspace.dependencies]`, next to the other internal crates (after `mixdog-tui-style = ...`):

    mixdog-tui = { path = "crates/mixdog-tui" }

## native/core/Cargo.lock

Refresh offline (`cargo metadata --offline --locked` will say what is missing; `cargo update --offline -w`). The crate adds no
package that is not already in the lock: its dependencies are workspace crates plus `unicode-segmentation`, `serde`,
`serde_json`, `tokio`, `tracing`, all already locked.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml

Run the workspace-hack refresh for the new member (the crate's Cargo.toml already carries the
`mixdog-workspace-hack = { version = "0.1", path = "../mixdog-workspace-hack" }` edge).

## Notes for the lead

* Dependency edges the crate takes: mixdog-term, mixdog-termtext, mixdog-tui-style, mixdog-markdown-ansi, mixdog-view-model,
  mixdog-session-view, mixdog-launch, mixdog-js, mixdog-fsio (all workspace members). mixdog-tui-widgets is added to this
  crate's Cargo.toml by nr-tui-surface-layout (wave 5), mixdog-core-session by nr-tui-footer (wave 6).
* The editor uses only `mixdog_js::JsRegex`, `mixdog_term::{KeyFlags, input::*}`, `mixdog_termtext::{display_width, wrap, grapheme}`,
  `mixdog_tui_style::Key` and `unicode_segmentation`; the other listed dependencies are for the stub modules' later tasks.
* No protocol method, no SERVICE_PENDING entry, no daemon registration: nothing here is served.
* Twin: `tests/editor_twin.rs` replays `tests/goldens/editor.json`; the golden was recorded with
  `node tests/recorders/record-editor.mjs --tree C:/Project/mixdog --write tests/goldens/editor.json` and is checked with
  `--check` (same command). The decoder corpus pairs come from `crates/mixdog-term/tests/goldens/keys.json`.
* `mixdog-testkit/tests/cfg_test_guard.rs` is not affected: mixdog-tui is not one of its LIBRARIES and its tests are
  `#[cfg(test)]` modules and an integration test.
